    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0328" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg254"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Sir F. Bruce</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>D<hi rendition="#small-caps">epartment of</hi> S<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">tate, Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 9, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to enclose for your
                    information a letter of the 21st ultimo, and its accompaniments, in regard to
                    the case of John McMahon, a Catholic priest, who, it appears, was arrested in
                    Canada by her Majesty’s authorities during the late Fenian invasion of that
                    province, and is now detained in prison in Toronto on suspicion of complicity
                    with the movement. It is stated in the papers which accompany this communication
                    that McMahon is a naturalized citizen of the United States, and that he is not a
                    member of the Fenian <pb facs="0329" n="255" xml:id="pg255"/> association. Under
                    these circumstances, I desire to avail myself of your good offices to bring the
                    matter to the attention of the government of Canada.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Hon. Sir <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frederick W. A. Bruce</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—I will thank you to return the original papers whenever you shall have
                        satisfied yourself as to their contents.</p>
                </postscript>




